            <ArticleTitle>Multifocal synchronous low-grade intramedullary and juxtacortical osteogenic sarcoma.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>265-70</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 41-year-old woman who presented with ipsilateral synchronous low-grade juxtacortical osteogenic sarcoma of the distal femur and low-grade intramedullary osteogenic sarcoma of the proximal tibia. The diagnosis and treatment and a review of the literature also are provided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
